---
/**
 * Privacy Policy (EU and UK GDPR, US state laws such as the CCPA/CPRA, COPPA). Source draft: docs/paddle/privacy-policy.md
 * (keep the two in sync). Not legal advice: a lawyer reviews it before the live Paddle account.
 * TODO (Ilan) items are marked inline: the processor list and the AI-training opt-outs (docs/paddle/ai-vendors.md).
 */
import LegalShell from "../components/pages/LegalShell.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config/site";
import { useCopy } from "../content/copy";
const { copy: COPY } = useCopy(Astro.url);
const l = COPY.legalPage;
const mail = SITE.email;
---

<LegalShell title="Privacy Policy" description="What personal data Tadam! collects, why, who it is shared with, how long we keep it and what your rights are under the GDPR and US state laws." updatedLine={`Last updated: ${l.privacyUpdated}`}>

  <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#who">Who we are</a></li>
      <li><a href="#collect">What we collect</a></li>
      <li><a href="#use">Why we use it</a></li>
      <li><a href="#share">Who we share it with</a></li>
      <li><a href="#transfers">International transfers</a></li>
      <li><a href="#keep">How long we keep it</a></li>
      <li><a href="#children">Children</a></li>
      <li><a href="#rights">Your rights</a></li>
      <li><a href="#cookies">Cookies</a></li>
      <li><a href="#security">Security</a></li>
      <li><a href="#changes">Changes</a></li>
      <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <section id="who">
    <h2 class="display">1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Tadam! is operated by {l.legalName}, a sole trader. We are the
      "controller" of the personal data described here. Contact us about privacy at <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="collect">
    <h2 class="display">2. What we collect</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Examples</th><th>Where it comes from</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Your account and order details</td><td>Name, email address, country</td><td>You, when you create a game and pay</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Payment details</td><td>Card or PayPal details, billing address</td><td>Collected and handled by <strong>Paddle</strong>, our merchant of record. We never see your full card number</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Game content</td><td>Stories, names, nicknames, details, photos and voice recordings about the guest of honor and other people</td><td>You, in the game creator</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Guest play data</td><td>The nickname a guest types to join, their answers and score</td><td>Guests, when they play. Guests don't need an account or email</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Messages to us</td><td>Your email address and what you write</td><td>You, when you email us</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Technical data</td><td>IP address, browser type, pages visited, error logs</td><td>Automatically, when you use the site</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Usage data (Google Analytics)</td><td>Pages viewed, buttons clicked, approximate location (city or country), device and browser type, how you found the site</td><td>Automatically, through Google Analytics, subject to your cookie choice (see <a href="#cookies">Cookies</a>)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Game content often includes information about <strong>other people, including children</strong>, such as the guest
      of honor at a bar mitzvah or birthday. You may only upload it if you have their permission, or their parent's or
      guardian's permission for children (see our <a href="/terms">Terms</a>). Please don't upload sensitive information
      such as health details, financial details or ID numbers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="use">
    <h2 class="display">3. Why we use it, and our legal basis (GDPR)</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Creating, delivering and supporting your game</td><td>Performance of our contract with you</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Processing payments, taxes and refunds (through Paddle)</td><td>Contract and legal obligation</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Keeping the Service secure and fixing errors</td><td>Legitimate interests</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Measuring how visitors use the site, to improve it (Google Analytics)</td><td>Consent in the EU, the UK and Switzerland; elsewhere, our legitimate interests</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sending service emails (your game link, receipts)</td><td>Contract</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Marketing emails, only if you opt in</td><td>Consent, which you can withdraw at any time</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      We don't sell your personal data, don't share it for cross-context behavioral advertising, and don't use your game
      content to train AI models ourselves.
    </p>
    {/* TODO (Ilan): once the opt-outs in docs/paddle/ai-vendors.md are confirmed (Base44, HeyGen, ElevenLabs), add back:
        "We have opted out of AI training with every provider that offers it, and we choose providers that don't train on customer data." */}
  </section>

  <section id="share">
    <h2 class="display">4. Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We use service providers ("processors") that handle data only on our instructions:</p>
    {/* TODO (Ilan): confirm the ElevenLabs location and which service sends the game-link emails (then add it as a row). */}
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>What for</th><th>Location</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Paddle.com</td><td>Payments, tax, refunds (Paddle is an independent controller for payment data)</td><td>UK / EU / US</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Netlify</td><td>Hosting the website</td><td>US</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Google (Google Analytics)</td><td>Measuring how visitors use the website</td><td>US</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Base44 (and the AI models it runs on)</td><td>Hosting the game creator and the games, drafting questions from your stories</td><td>US</td></tr>
          <tr><td>ElevenLabs</td><td>The host's synthetic voice reading your game's script</td><td>US</td></tr>
          <tr><td>HeyGen</td><td>The host's video</td><td>US</td></tr>
          <tr><td>BytePlus (Seedance)</td><td>Video generation</td><td>Malaysia, Indonesia and/or the EU</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Forward Email and Google (Gmail)</td><td>Receiving and answering the emails you send us</td><td>US</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>We may also disclose data if the law requires it, or to protect our rights.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="transfers">
    <h2 class="display">5. International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      We and some of our providers process data outside the EU and UK, including in the US. Where data leaves the EU or UK, we rely on adequacy decisions,
      the EU-US Data Privacy Framework where the provider is certified, or Standard Contractual Clauses.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="keep">
    <h2 class="display">6. How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Game content and the game itself:</strong> 30 days from delivery, then deleted. You can ask us to delete it sooner.</li>
      <li><strong>Order records:</strong> as long as tax and accounting law requires (generally up to 7 years). These records don't include your game content.</li>
      {/* TODO (Ilan): replace with the real log retention once known. */}
      <li><strong>Technical logs:</strong> kept by our hosting providers for a limited time to run and secure the Service, then deleted.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="children">
    <h2 class="display">7. Children</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is for adults (18+) organizing events. We don't knowingly let children create games or give us their
      personal data directly. Children may play as guests by typing a nickname, without giving an email or creating an
      account. Information about children that a parent includes in a game is used only to make that game and is deleted
      after 30 days. If you believe a child has given us personal data directly, write to
      {" "}<a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a> and we'll delete it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="rights">
    <h2 class="display">8. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you can ask to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>access the data we hold about you, or get a copy of it</li>
      <li>correct it</li>
      <li>delete it</li>
      <li>restrict or object to how we use it</li>
      <li>withdraw consent at any time, where we rely on consent</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>EU and UK residents</strong> can also complain to their local data protection authority.</p>
    <p>
      <strong>California and other US state residents</strong> have the right to know, delete and correct their data,
      and to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal data. We don't sell or share personal data in that sense. We
      won't treat you differently for using your rights.
    </p>
    <p>To use any right, write to <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>. We reply within 30 days.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="cookies">
    <h2 class="display">9. Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      We use the cookies and similar storage the site needs to work (for example, to keep your game draft while you
      create it), and Google Analytics to understand how visitors use the site. We don't use advertising cookies, and we
      have turned off Google's advertising features and Google signals.
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Cookie</th><th>Set by</th><th>What for</th><th>Kept for</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code></td><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Telling visits apart and counting them, so we see which pages and buttons are used</td><td>Up to 2 years</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      <strong>In the EU, the UK and Switzerland</strong>, Google Analytics sets no cookies unless you click "Accept" on
      the cookie banner. Until then, and if you decline, Google receives only cookieless signals (for example, that a
      page was viewed) without an identifier for your device. <strong>Elsewhere</strong>, analytics cookies are on by
      default and you can turn them off at any time.
    </p>
    <p>
      To change your choice, use <button type="button" class="link-btn" data-cookie-settings>Cookie settings</button>
      (also in the footer of every page). Google Analytics data is kept for 14 months. You can also block cookies in
      your browser or install Google's
      {" "}<a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="security">
    <h2 class="display">10. Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use encryption in transit (HTTPS), access controls and reputable providers. Game links are private and hard to
      guess, but anyone with the link can open the game, so share it only with your guests.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2 class="display">11. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy. The date at the top shows the latest version. If a change is significant, we'll tell you
      by email or on the site.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2 class="display">12. Contact</h2>
    <ul class="contact">
      <li>{l.legalName}</li>
      <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</LegalShell>

<style>
  .link-btn { padding: 0; border: 0; background: none; color: inherit; font: inherit; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; cursor: pointer; }
</style>
